WEBVTT

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:11.650
Short and sweet number 12. In a situation where it was possible that a non-mevushal open bottle of wine was touched by a non-Jew, it depends on the type of non-Jew who possibly touched it.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:21.090
If it was possibly touched by a Christian, so then Rav Ovadya told us that for the Sfardim, the wine is forbidden to drink and even to get benefit from, while the Rama held that wine would be permissible.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.910
If it was possibly touched by a Muslim, everybody agreed that the wine is permitted.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:36.710
We then discussed the question of irreligious Jews, particularly Jews who are Mechalei Shabbos B'Far Hesya, which means that they desecrate Shabbos publicly in front of ten people at least three times.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:48.890
So then we know that for the Din of the Gemara, that any wine that is touched by a Mechalei Shabbos B'Far Hesya, the wine is forbidden to drink, but it still is permitted to get benefit from.

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.850
However, again, we cannot drink it.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:58.130
Or Shternbach does tell us that it's best not to get benefit from the wine if there's no need, but the minimal is that the wine would be prohibited to drink.

00:00:58.270 --> 00:01:02.870
We discussed what is considered a Michal Shabbos B'Far Hesya b'Zman Hazet in current times.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:08.130
So we said that there are really basically, in the general sense, there are four types of irreligious Jews.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:09.990
The first type is the traditional Jew.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:16.990
That would be someone who, although they are not Shabbos observant, they will go to shul, they recite Kiddush, they will do traditional practices.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:20.650
However, they just don't keep Shabbos and they transgress it publicly.

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:25.030
The next category was what we call the respectful Jew.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.290
That's someone who, again, they do not keep Shabbos.

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:32.350
They will be Michal Shabbos before Heser in public, but they would not do so in front of a Rav or someone that they respect.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:36.690
The third category was the totally unaffiliated Jew or the Tinov SheNizhba.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.310
They do not have a Jewish upbringing.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.570
They do not have a Jewish education.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.690
They will deliberately transgress Shabbos even in front of a Rav.

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:50.690
But again, they're not doing it out of spite, they just did not have the proper education or sensitivity to Shabbos.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:55.990
The last category was the Mummer L'Hachas, a person who is the anti-religious Jew.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:02.710
He had a Jewish education, they rejected it, and are now deliberately transgressing Shabbos, and they would do so even in front of a Rav.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:08.010
So the status of the first three, the traditional Jews, the respectful Jews, and the Tinek Shinizhba,

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:12.950
we said was a machlokas between the poskim, whether or not they would prohibit wine that they touched.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:22.130
However, we did say that the Mumra L'Chachis, this anti-religious Jew, if he would touch wine, everybody agrees that is a case that the wine would be forbidden to drink.
